<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1" ProductVersion="3.1.4024.12">
  <DUT Name="ST_ViciControl" Id="{3dbe2ab7-c9fe-4a0a-8fa6-39ab515d681c}">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    ST_ViciControl - control (command) interface of one multi-port Vici
    selector valve reached over RS-232.

    PURPOSE
        Groups the values FB_ViciDriver needs in order to talk to a Vici valve:
        which valve on the serial bus to address (iAddress), which port it
        should route to (iReqPos) and how many ports the valve has
        (iPortCount). It is the control half of the Vici driver interface; the
        reply and position-readback half is ST_ViciStatus. Two members carried
        over from the initial commit (sViciReply, xDirection) are not used by
        any POU today and are documented as such below.

    USAGE
        Declared as a plain instance and handed to FB_ViciDriver.i_stControl:
            FB_ViciValve.stViciVlvCtrl - filled each scan from the iAddress,
                iReqPos and iNumOfPorts inputs of that block;
            FB_SelectorM3.stSelector.astViciVlvCtrl[1..2] - one instance per
                valve on the shared M3-selector serial bus, iAddress set to the
                valve index (1 or 2) and iReqPos taken from iVici1ReqPos /app/namespaces/d6f73763-31bc-4bea-8f49-b5906058e129/
                iVici2ReqPos after a LIMIT(1, ..., 12) clamp; iPortCount is
                left at its default of 12 there.
        The type carries no pytmc pragma, so it is not published to EPICS
        directly: the operator-facing PVs are declared on the blocks that own
        the structure (FB_12PortVici and FB_4PortViciValve expose iReqPos and
        SampleNames).

    OBJECTIVES
        - One named structure instead of individual FB terminals, so the driver
          signature and its callers stay stable when a field is added
          (iPortCount was added this way, to support 4-port valves).
        - Make the port numbering explicit: iReqPos is the logical 1-based port
          number used throughout this library, and FB_ViciDriver converts it to
          the vendor's numbering with iPortCount + 1 - iReqPos before it sends a
          'GO<port>' command, converting the 'CP' readback back the same way.

    PRECONDITIONS
        - iReqPos must be within 1..iPortCount. FB_ViciDriver does clamp an
          out-of-range request (i_stControl.iReqPos := LIMIT(1, ..., iPortCount))
          before it commands a move, but that clamp runs only once a move is
          already being sequenced, so a caller must bound-check the request it
          writes into this structure.
        - iPortCount must match the valve actually fitted: 12 on the 12-port
          model, 4 on the 4-port model (which overrides the default through
          FB_ViciValve.iNumOfPorts). It sets both the clamp range and the mirror
          arithmetic iPortCount + 1 - n used to convert between the library's
          port numbering and the vendor's, so a wrong value silently addresses
          the wrong port.
        - iAddress must be unique per valve on the serial bus: two instances
          with the same address answer each other's commands and both
          FB_ViciDriver reply checks fail.

    UNITS
        None - every member is a count, an index or a boolean. Port numbers are
        dimensionless 1-based positions, sViciReply is a character string and
        xDirection a boolean flag.

    HISTORY
        2023-05-19 J. Zamudio - type added with sViciReply, iReqPos, xDirection
            and iAddress in the initial commit (746deac); no member documented.
        2024-06-25 J. Zamudio - iPortCount added with the default 12 to
            generalise FB_ViciDriver for 4-port valves while keeping 12-port
            behaviour unchanged (8390105).
        2025-05-29 J. Zamudio - moved to sample-delivery/Library/DUTs/Vici in
            the project restructure (9b2fb2c); contents unchanged.
        2026-11-27 Scirix Agent - added this header and one comment per member
            (audit finding 452, task 362); no member, type or default changed.
*)
TYPE ST_ViciControl :
STRUCT
    // UNUSED - no POU reads or writes this member. The reply text of a serial
    // transaction is kept in ST_ViciStatus.sViciReply, written by FB_ViciDriver
    // from FB_ViciTransaction.q_sResponseData. Carried over from the initial
    // commit; left in place so the structure layout and the FB_ViciDriver
    // interface stay unchanged. STRING, no unit.
    sViciReply			: STRING;

    // Requested port of the valve: the logical 1-based position the valve
    // should route to, range 1..iPortCount, in this library's port numbering.
    // FB_ViciDriver compares it with the last commanded position and, when they
    // differ, converts it to the vendor's numbering with
    // iPortCount + 1 - iReqPos and sends the resulting 'GO<port>' command.
    // Written every scan by FB_ViciValve from its iReqPos input, and by
    // FB_SelectorM3 for the selector valves. Port number, no unit.
    iReqPos				: INT;

    // UNUSED - no POU reads or writes this member. FB_ViciDriver does not pick
    // a travel direction: it always commands the vendor's mirrored position
    // (iPortCount + 1 - iReqPos) and the valve reaches it by its own shortest
    // path. Carried over from the initial commit; left in place so the
    // structure layout stays unchanged. Boolean flag, no unit.
    xDirection			: BOOL;

    // RS-232 address of this valve on the serial bus it shares with the other
    // valves. Passed to FB_ViciTransaction as the command address and used to
    // build the reply prefix FB_ViciDriver expects back, so the 'CP' readback
    // of valve 1 must start with '1CP', that of valve 2 with '2CP', and so on.
    // FB_ViciValve sets it from its iAddress input; FB_SelectorM3 sets it to
    // the valve index (1 or 2) on the shared M3 bus. Bus address, no unit.
    iAddress			: INT;

    // Number of ports fitted on the valve: 12 on the 12-port model (this
    // default, kept for backward compatibility) and 4 on the 4-port model,
    // which overrides it through FB_ViciValve.iNumOfPorts. Sets the valid
    // iReqPos range 1..iPortCount and the mirror arithmetic
    // iPortCount + 1 - n used to convert between this library's port numbering
    // and the vendor's. Port count, no unit.
    iPortCount			: INT := 12;
END_STRUCT
END_TYPE
]]></Declaration>
  </DUT>
</TcPlcObject>